    "created_at": "2016-04-05T12:46:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-05T12:46:49Z",
    "body": "So we'll have three origins, right? `location.origin`, `document.origin`, and `origin`? Will they always return the same value, or not? Should we add examples of how they could differ? Should we add warnings to the two that we don't like?\n",
